## 🛠️ 2. Universal Dispatch Script (`generate_image.py`)

A standalone, multi-backend Python runner is provided in `scripts/generate_image.py`:

```bash
# Generate using Gemini Imagen 3 (requires GEMINI_API_KEY)
python3 scripts/generate_image.py --backend gemini --style imagen3 --prompt "A sleek titanium cybernetic watch"

# Generate using OpenAI DALL-E 3 (requires OPENAI_API_KEY)
python3 scripts/generate_image.py --backend openai --style dalle3 --prompt "An isometric cozy coffee shop diorama"

# Generate local SVG vector graphics (Zero API / 100% offline)
python3 scripts/generate_image.py --backend local-svg --prompt "Shield and sword emblem" --output shield.svg

# Generate local game texture with Pillow (Zero API / 100% offline)
python3 scripts/generate_image.py --backend local-texture --type noise --output noise_texture.png
```

---

## 🖥️ 3. Local Offline Generation (Zero API Required)

When no external API keys are configured, generate crisp vector graphics and game textures locally using Python and Pillow:

```python
from PIL import Image, ImageDraw

def create_badge(output_path="badge.png"):
    img = Image.new("RGBA", (512, 512), (0, 0, 0, 0))
    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(img)
    # Render procedural vector shapes or icons
    draw.rounded_rectangle([32, 32, 480, 480], radius=64, fill=(30, 41, 59), outline=(56, 189, 248), width=8)
    img.save(output_path, "PNG")
```

